    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d904">

                <pb facs="1090" n="980" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg980"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1111 Halverstadt, Harriet/8: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-12-31T12:00:00+08:00">December 31,
                        1931—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received December 31—2:30 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1160. Legation 1133, December 27, 11 a.m., and Foochow’s December 29, 1
                        p.m.<anchor n="79" xml:id="d904-f1"/> Following from American Consul General
                    at Nanking: <pb facs="1091" n="981" xml:id="pg981"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“December 30, 4 p.m. I have orally informed the Foreign Office today of
                            the above telegram and have strongly represented the gravity of the
                            situation. The Foreign Office has received from Foochow a detailed
                            report of measures taken for the release of Miss Halverstadt which will
                            be copied to me. I have been promised that renewed instructions of an
                            urgent character will be sent by the National Government to the Fukien
                                authorities.”<anchor n="80" xml:id="d904-f2"/></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d904-f1" n="79" xml:id="d904-f1-content">
                <p>Latter not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d904-f2" n="80" xml:id="d904-f2-content">
                <p>Miss Halverstadt’s release was effected on January 3, 1932 (393.1111 Halverstadt,
                    Harriet/25).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
